{"source":"github","project_id":"academydatasets","target":"rstudio/academyDatasets","id":"issue/77","ref":77,"title":"Description of `rideshare` data set","description":"The current  description of the `rideshare` data set reads:\r\n\r\n\u003e This dataset contains various hourly time series representations of attributes related to Uber and Lyft rideshare services for various locations in New York between 2018-11-26 and 2018-12-18. For a given starting location, provider and service,\r\n\r\nA couple problems here: \r\n1. This refers to New York, but these observations are actually about Uber and Lyft rides in Boston (this mistake originated in the [description on zenodo](https://zenodo.org/record/5122114#.YfSFJfXMLVa) ([this source](https://www.kaggle.com/ravi72munde/uber-lyft-cab-prices) confirms that is data is about Boston -- I only just noticed that one of the `source_location`s is \"Boston University\" 😬)\r\n\r\n2. The description contains an incomplete clause at the end that should be removed. This seems to also be carried over from the description on zenodo:\r\n\r\n\u003eFor a given starting location, provider and service, the following types are represented: 'price_min', 'price_mean', 'price_max', 'distance_min', 'distance_mean', 'distance_max', 'surge_min', 'surge_mean', 'surge_max', 'api_calls', 'temp', 'rain', 'humidity', 'clouds' and 'wind'.","published_at":"2022-01-29T00:32:49Z","url":"https://github.com/rstudio/academyDatasets/issues/77","type":"issue","extra":{"author":"brendanhcullen","state":"OPEN"}}
