{"source":"github","project_id":"academydatasets","target":"rstudio/academyDatasets","id":"issue/29","ref":29,"title":"`describe_dataset()` gives unhelpful types","description":"Currently, `describe_datset()` uses `typeof()` to describe column types, which gives unhelpful descriptions for all but the most common of data types. For example, `describe_datset()` labels factors as `integer` and times as `double`. I propose using `vctrs::vec_ptype_abbr()` to describe column types. This is the same function used to give column types in `tibble`, so its output should be both comprehensive and familiar.","published_at":"2021-08-05T18:14:21Z","updated_at":"2021-08-24T17:31:10Z","url":"https://github.com/rstudio/academyDatasets/issues/29","type":"issue","extra":{"author":"rossellhayes","state":"CLOSED"}}
